 "text": "Most British soldiers who died in the Crimean War weren't killed by wounds, so what killed them? In Florence Nightingale's chart, blue is death from preventable disease. After a sanitary commission flushed sewers in 1 ,855, the blue shrank, even the next winter. Strong evidence not certainty. One chart can't rule out other changes. Lesson, before calling it proof, ask what else changed. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
